+      "pin_review_2026_08_20_lane161": "PIN STILL HELD at 64d528be7; the queue lane-156 left is now TWO, not three. The real unreviewed surface re-derived at this fetch is unchanged: git rev-list --count --no-merges 64d528be7..ciru/main --not rocmfpx/HEAD upstream/master = 15 (currency's 315 remains the triple-counting artifact lane-156 refuted). NEW THIS LANE: c14872f84 'chat: trim messages sent to StepFun parser' - lane-156's one UNKNOWN - is CLOSED AS DUPLICATE, shown not assumed: its own commit message names it a port of upstream 2d973636e, git merge-base --is-ancestor 2d973636e b10524 returns 0, and trim_all_content plus the StepFun source-marker check are already live in our common/chat.cpp at lines 3163/3612 (arrived with this lane's own b10524 bump). REMAINING QUEUE: 66afd2128 + 0d313da18 stay blocked-TAKE exactly as lane-156 measured (per-hunk judgment across ~18 files against our different model files - a lane, not a rung), and 9d91bc168 stays behind the President's DualView park plus this rig's lack of CUDA. The pin cannot advance while blocked TAKEs remain; the runbook allows re-pin only for SKIP.",
+      "pin_review_2026_08_18_lane156": "PIN DELIBERATELY HELD at 64d528be7, and the number this row has been carrying is REFUTED. `currency` prints 'BEHIND by 315 commit(s)'. That is a range count WITH merges over a fork that is a SIBLING OF ROCmFPX AND A MIRROR OF UPSTREAM, so it triple-counts. Lane-156 re-derived it in three subtractions, each one command, all banked in research/local-inference/lane-evidence/2026-08-18-lane-156-currency2-proofs/goal5-ciru-real-delta.txt: `git rev-list --count --no-merges 64d528be7..ciru/main` = 274 (merges removed); `... --not rocmfpx/HEAD` = 129 (ciru-ai/ROCmFPX and charlie12345/ROCmFPX are the SAME PROJECT in two orgs, and that history is already covered by the reviewed `rocmfpx` pin, which is CURRENT); `... --not rocmfpx/HEAD upstream/master` = 15. FIFTEEN is the real unreviewed surface, not 315. ALL 15 ARE REVIEWED HERE. (a) FIVE ARE ALREADY IN OUR BASE - 01de1b421 (#26177), f15469a6f (#25832), 8a33d67b7 (#25830), 50265ff2a (#25643), 9307bd974 (#25611) are upstream cherry-picks, and each was found by `git log --grep` inside b10488: 0324696b8, dee2a846b, 2cfc7670e, c812c543f, 8bb909374. DUPLICATE, closed by this lane's bump itself. (b) FOUR ARE DOC/README MASS-DUMPS - b51512581, 09628016e, 36d659e1e (735/123 README plus ~4400 lines of docs/, a Dockerfile and CI), 112629f1e (179/682 README). NOISE. (c) 9b21a5512 is ONE CI line. NOISE. (d) 8ffb2cd5a's Vulkan half is DUPLICATE: its `find_package(SPIRV-Headers CONFIG QUIET)` fallback plus GGML_VULKAN_SPIRV_HEADERS_INCLUDE_DIR is already in our ggml/src/ggml-vulkan/CMakeLists.txt - lane-152 took it (series patch 0332) - CHECKED by string count (QUIET 1, the fallback var 3, the old CONFIG REQUIRED 0). Its remaining half is 24/5 in ggml-cuda.cu, off-rig. (e) c14872f84 'chat: trim messages sent to StepFun parser' - a common/chat.cpp parser fix with 50 lines of test; a real candidate, UNKNOWN against our chat.cpp and NOT closed here. (f) 9d91bc168 'Checkpoint tested DualView research r