+      "pin_review_2026_08_27_take_ports": "PIN DELIBERATELY HELD at 39d97a876. The four TAKE commits ruled by research/local-inference/2026-08-27-buun-deep-review.md were adapted onto this tree; three are SKIPPED on a DEFECT-PRESENCE check the review itself listed as owed, one is PORTED IN PART. (1) e332b2494 'dflash: harden checkpoint rewind lifecycle' - PORTED IN PART: common_prompt_checkpoint::try_load_dft (the non-aborting draft-image restore) plus its three server call sites, which previously GGML_ABORT'ed the whole process on an incompatible draft image. NOT taken: common_speculative_sequence_event / _sequence_transition and both impl overrides - they mutate buun-only drafter state (stash/positions/adpt/pregate_*/carry_rows_per_seq and common_speculative_impl_dflash::ring_state_reset), none of which exists in our common/speculative.cpp (Grep: 0 hits); porting the enum alone would be a dispatcher with zero overrides and zero callers. The cross-ring-interleave.cu leg is CUDA, off-rig, dropped. (2) 2714303b5 'server: repair speculative state after cache restores' - SKIPPED, defect ABSENT: its real fix is the dft_pos0 discontinuity fail-safe inside buun's draft_dflash rebase machinery (pstate.target_base / dft_pos_max / 'precedes drafter base'), and our tree has no target_base or dft_pos0 at all (Grep over common/: 0 hits; the 4 dft_pos_max hits are the unrelated eagle3 cross-ubatch bridge). The HTTP 500 it converts to a cold rebase is not reachable here. The rest of the commit renames the enum from (1) and wires composite_image_restored through VBR artifact companions. (3) 92eef392a 'server: fix MTP and mmproj swap fit accounting' - SKIPPED, substrate ABSENT: it repairs buun's mmproj-GPU-swap fixed-point fit solver, and our server-context.cpp has none of mmproj_gpu_swap / swap_fit_solved / n_ctx_fit / hp_nct_mtp / n_seq_max_full / DFLASH_VERIFY_OUTPUTS_PER_SEQ (Grep: 0 hits) - our fit path is the upstream one that adds mmproj/draft sizes to fit_params_target. The common/ half is a VBR growth-headroom param (cparams.vbr_dynamic, absent) plus common_model_uses_recurrent_memory, which has no caller without the server half. (4) 9d0d4b650 'vbr: restore dynamic partial-offload KV placement' - SKIPPED, and the review's 'no VBR symbols despite its vbr: prefix' claim is REFUTED: the 54 lines are entirely VBR-substrate - vbr_params_, vbr_layer_policy, cpu_bound_kv, try_vmm_alloc, ggml_type_is_turbo - and our src/llama-kv-cache.cpp contains none of the five (Grep: 0 hits). The review checked for llama-vbr* FILENAMES, not for the symbols the hunks use. Conservatism proof for the whole wave: git diff --numstat arifi/main..ingest/buun-2026-08-27 over 'ggml/src/ggml-vulkan/*' '*vulkan*' '*.comp' 'ggml/include/ggml.h' is EMPTY, so F-138's reorder fix and the TQ3/TURBO id block are untouched. Buckets 3/4/5 (VBR prompt-cache CONFLICT, decayed-frequency retention, the HIP commit) are unchanged and still owed; the re-pin stays unlawful under runbook 3 while they stand. Report: research/local-inference/2026-08-27-buun-take-ports-report.md.",
+      "pin_review_2026_08_21_patch0394_backfill": "BACKFILL, written 2026-08-27 for an ingestion that happened on 2026-08-21 without one. Series patch 0394-dflash-ingest-buun-s-DFlash2-adaptive-controller-bui (commit b95c9e637) took buun's DFlash2 adaptive controller, per-sequence state, the 8->13 block-size metadata mapping, the DFlash2 pre-flight sizing draft.n_max, and explicit-depth tracking - content from 396469835..1ab12e269, i.e. commits INSIDE the then-unreviewed 39d97a876..head surface - while this pin stayed at 39d97a876 and no pin_review row was written. Its own trailer says 'Origin: ArifiLabs (native), integrating github.com/spiritbuun/buun-llama-cpp 396469835..1ab12e269'. VERDICT AS INGESTED: taken, built, and then defaulted OFF by measurement (16 prompts: fixed cap 3 = 6.59 t/s clean vs reactive/buun = 4.04 t/s with 8/16 degenerate); both policies stay reachable behind GGML_DFLASH2_ADAPTIVE / GGML_DFLASH2_PREVENTIVE. Series patch 0397 later added our three defect fixes on top. The pin did NOT move and MUST NOT be read as having moved: the ingest was partial and the remaining 39d97a876..2174ad63b surface was still unreviewed until 2026-08-27. Second defect corrected at the same time: licenses/buun-MIT.txt did not exist while buun-derived code was already on arifi/main - retained 2026-08-27, row added to licenses/README.md.",
