+      "pin_review_2026_08_18_lane154": "PIN ADVANCED f6124e914 -> 7ebcbb0b6 (feature/turboquant-kv-cache, 2026-08-17). THIS REVIEW SUPERSEDES TWO NUMBERS IN THE lane-143 KEY ABOVE. (1) Its merge-base 1fd6dfe9f is STALE: upstream/master has advanced to 7acdbb1f1, so merge-base(f6124e914, upstream/master) is now 15586e2d7 and the 816 non-merge figure reads 848 today. Range counts are NOT comparable across an upstream move; reachability counts are, which is why the 151 reproduces EXACTLY: git rev-list --count --no-merges 1fd6dfe9f..f6124e914 --not upstream/master = 151. The backlog of record at this pin is git rev-list --count --no-merges 7ebcbb0b6 --not upstream/master = 183 (151 + 32 new). (2) The 33 turbo/TQ quant-and-kernel figure was counted at the old pin and is NOT carried forward; lane-154 re-derived the ranked core from its own numstat instead. WHAT LANDED, with proofs: the VK-MOE-CACHE cluster - the Vulkan MoE expert-cache provider, three files absent from our tree outright (ggml/src/ggml-moe-cache-common.h, ggml/src/ggml-vulkan/ggml-vulkan-moe-cache.cpp +1740, ggml/src/ggml-vulkan/vulkan-shaders/moe_cache_mv.comp +903) plus the +56/-0 addition to ggml/src/ggml-backend-moe-cache.h, four Vulkan handle accessors, and 23 shader variants. Taken at TIP state, not replayed - 539e98959 rewrites what 6723fdfa8 and f3042492d introduced. Also landed: f0420e056, the V-unpad head count derived from the tensor, at all three sites. THE INGEST EXPOSED A ROOT DEFECT IN OUR OWN TREE, now fixed: our ggml-vulkan.cpp included ggml-vulkan.h BEFORE <vulkan/vulkan_core.h>, the reverse of the source fork, so any declaration guarded on #if defined(VK_VERSION_1_0) was invisible there and its definition silently took C++ linkage. It presents as a LINK error, never a compile error. WHAT WAS DECLINED, LOUDLY: 7f8302613 (turbo3 extern) is BROKEN for us - lane-143 already refuted it and our self-refutation is committed at 006d7837c. 12 rows are absent but every missing code line is CUDA/Metal/SYCL/HIP: NOT dropped, escalated to HQ, because the rig has no such device and the F-107 and backend-ops proofs are therefore unobtainable. ~20 further CAPABILITY rows were NOT attempted this wave - each keeps its verdict, its evidence cell and an explicit outcome in research/local-inference/2026-08-18-turboquant-disposition.md, which carries all 183 rows and is regenerable by classify.py + coverage.py + disposition.py. PROOFS: build green by exe mtime; test-backend-ops 26213/26260 identical to the banked baseline and compared CASE-FOR-CASE (3 in / 3 out, all inside the two runbook-named flaky bands); arifi_sync_check.py GREEN, and shown RED on a planted violation. PIN HONESTY, recorded rather than smoothed over: while this lane ran, the live checkout advanced again to d14e36827. The pin records the sha I ACTUALLY REVIEWED (7ebcbb0b6), so currency will read BEHIND by exactly 3 fork-authored commits - 730cc87ed (moe-cache: heat-protected eviction keeps hot experts resident), cef75bf06 (docs split of the THROTTLE rule) and d14e36827 (docs: AI-assisted contribution workflows). Re-pinning past unreviewed commits to clear the row is the exact thing the gate exists to stop, and UPDATE-RUNBOOK 3 says so: UNKNOWN means leave BEHIND and say so. Live-head fork-authored total for the next lane: 186. HQ RULING 2026-08-18, EXECUTED: the 12 off-rig rows are LANDED UNBUILT (engine b5076671) rather than held - aa606e4a9, 78104ec46, f31e9b7c7, fa7393cd8, 2603f5d98, abbe07788, 7a2b25a0c, 1f8ceb051, 7b4192ad7, f050a2501, a577aebfb, ccd29136c. STATUS IS BUILD-UNPROVEN: this rig has no CUDA/Metal/SYCL/HIP device, so no F-107 exe proof and no backend-ops execution proof exists for any of them, and none is claimed. They cannot reach the rig build - CMakeCache has those six backends BOOL=OFF and build.ninja has zero compiling references to their directories - and the rig build plus arifi_sync_check.py are GREEN after landing, which proves only that they touch nothing here. Landed by t